et',\n  379: 'Silicon Mainnet',\n  30379: 'Silicon Mainnet',\n  383: 'Plasma Mainnet',\n  30383: 'Plasma Mainnet',\n  389: 'Gate Layer Mainnet',\n  30389: 'Gate Layer Mainnet',\n  386: 'zkVerify Mainnet',\n  30386: 'zkVerify Mainnet',\n  388: '0G Mainnet',\n  30388: '0G Mainnet',\n  390: 'Monad Mainnet',\n  30390: 'Monad Mainnet',\n  391: 'Ethereal Mainnet',\n  30391: 'Ethereal Mainnet',\n  392: 'OpenLedger Mainnet',\n  30392: 'OpenLedger Mainnet',\n  395: 'Nexera Mainnet',\n  30395: 'Nexera Mainnet',\n  30423: 'IOTA L1 Mainnet',\n  396: 'Stable Mainnet',\n  30396: 'Stable Mainnet',\n  399: 'Horizen Mainnet',\n  30399: 'Horizen Mainnet',\n  402: 'Redbelly Mainnet',\n  30402: 'Redbelly Mainnet',\n  403: 'Citrea Mainnet',\n  30403: 'Citrea Mainnet',\n  10439: 'Tempo Testnet',\n  40439: 'Tempo Testnet',\n  40500: 'Starknet Sepolia Testnet',\n  398: 'MegaETH Mainnet',\n  30398: 'MegaETH Mainnet',\n  420: 'Tron Mainnet',\n  406: 'Kite Mainnet',\n  30406: 'Kite Mainnet',\n  407: 'Pharos Mainnet',\n  408: 'Irys Mainnet',\n  409: 'Chiliz Mainnet',\n  30407: 'Pharos Mainnet',\n  30408: 'Irys Mainnet',\n  30409: 'Chiliz Mainnet',\n  381: 'Camp Mainnet',\n  30381: 'Camp Mainnet',\n  385: 'Dinari Mainnet',\n  30385: 'Dinari Mainnet',\n  394: 'Injective EVM Mainnet',\n  30394: 'Injective EVM Mainnet',\n  397: 'Zama Mainnet',\n  30397: 'Zama Mainnet',\n  393: 'Doma Mainnet',\n  30393: 'Doma Mainnet',\n  401: 'Rise Mainnet',\n  30401: 'Rise Mainnet',\n  413: 'AULT Mainnet',\n  30413: 'AULT Mainnet',\n  414: 'Neo X Mainnet',\n  30414: 'Neo X Mainnet',\n  415: 'Rayls Mainnet',\n  30415: 'Rayls Mainnet',\n  416: 'Robinhood Chain Mainnet',\n  30416: 'Robinhood Chain Mainnet',\n  417: 'Arc Mainnet',\n  30417: 'Arc Mainnet',\n};\n\nexport const NOTES = {\n\n  40161:\n    'LayerZero Testnet Endpoints use the real Mainnet pricefeed for cross-chain transfers. That means Ethereum Sepolia uses the real Ethereum gwei price. For testing EVM \u003c\u003e EVM transfers, it may be cheaper to use another EVM testnet with a cheaper cost of blockspace.',\n\n  30165:\n    'zkSync uses its own compiler called zkSync-solc, which generates different bytecode than the standard Solidity compiler (solc).',\n  40305:\n    'zkSync uses its own compiler called zkSync-solc, which generates different bytecode than the standard Solidity compiler (solc).',\n  30420:\n    'TRX, the native token of Tron, uses 6 decimals, which affects how transactions and gas fees are calculated and can require specific handling in smart contracts and dApps.',\n  40420:\n    'TRX, the native token of Tron, uses 6 decimals, which affects how transactions and gas fees are calculated and can require specific handling in smart contracts and dApps.',\n  30230:\n    'Shimmer, while being EVM-like, uses a different approach to gas token decimals, which could lead to specific implementations and adjustments in your gas calculations and transactions.',\n  30273:\n    'The Skale Endpoint uses an alternative ERC20 token instead of the native gas token for omnichain fees. You will need to modify your _payNative() function in OApp to handle ERC20 fees (see OFTAlt).',\n  273: 'The Skale Endpoint uses an alternative ERC20 token instead of the native gas token for omnichain fees. You will need to modify LzApp to handle ERC20 fees.',\n  40273:\n    'The Skale Endpoint uses an alternative ERC20 token instead of the native gas token for omnichain fees.  You will need to modify your _payNative() function in OApp to handle ERC20 fees (see OFTAlt).',\n  40285:\n    'The Hedera EVM has 8 decimals while their JSON RPC uses 18 decimals for `msg.value`, please take precaution when calling `quoteFee`',\n  10285:\n    'The Hedera EVM has 8 decimals while their JSON RPC uses 18 decimals for `msg.value`, please take precaution when calling `quoteFee`',\n  30154:\n    'The Ethereum Sepolia Mainnet Endpoint is a connection between Sepolia Testnet and LayerZero Mainnet Endpoints. This should NOT be used for testing connections to other testnet networks.',\n  30385:\n    'The Dinari Endpoint uses an alternative ERC20 token instead of the native gas token for omnichain fees. You will need to modify your _payNative() function in OApp to handle ERC20 fees (see OFTAlt).',\n  385: 'The Dinari Endpoint uses an alternative ERC20 token instead of the native gas token for omnichain fees. You will need to modify LzApp to handle ERC20 fees.',\n  30398:\n    'MegaETH uses a multidimensional gas model (https://docs.megaeth.com/megaevm#multidimensional-gas-model), there are two gas costs associated with any given transaction - compute gas and storage gas. What this means for developers is that you should estimate the gas costs for MegaETH transactions beforehand and make sure you set enforcedOptions with the estimated amount + some buffer. As per our calculations - 250k gas should be sufficient.',\n  30390:\n    'Monad charges users based on the gas limit specified in the transaction, not the actual gas used (https://docs.monad.xyz/developer-essentials/gas-pricing#gas-limit-not-gas-used). Additionally, Monad has repriced certain opcodes for cold state access - cold account access costs 10,100 gas (vs 2,600 on Ethereum) and cold storage access costs 8,100 gas (vs 2,100 on Ethereum) (https://docs.monad.xyz/developer-essentials/opcode-pricing). Developers should estimate gas costs for Monad transactions beforehand and set enforcedOptions with appropriately higher gas limits to account for these differences.',\n  30280:\n    'Sei raised the SSTORE opcode gas cost from 20,000 to 72,000. Any transaction that writes to storage on Sei now costs more gas, including lzReceive calls. If your OApp hardcodes gas limits in enforced options for messages to Sei, increase them by at least 55,000 from the default 80,000 or transactions will revert. Frontends using estimateGas are unaffected, but review any fixed gas values in your on-chain or off-chain configs.',\n};\nexport const DEPRECATED_CHAINS = [\n  'base-goerli',\n  'goerli',\n  'zksync-testnet',\n  'masa',\n  'masa-testnet',\n  'eon', // Horizen EON - deprecated\n  'eon-testnet', // Horizen EON Testnet - deprecated\n  'okx', // OKX Mainnet - deprecated\n  'swell',\n  'swellchain',\n  'swell-testnet',\n  'swellchain-testnet',\n  'zklink',\n  'zklink-nova',\n  'bevm',\n  'bevm-testnet',\n  'sagaevm',\n  'sagaevm-testnet',\n  'homeverse',\n  'homeverse-testnet',\n  'bahamut',\n  'bahamut-testnet',\n  'mp1', // Corn\n  'mp1-testnet',\n  'zkevm', // Polygon zkEVM\n  'zkevm-testnet', // Polygon zkEVM Testnet\n  'zkpolygon',\n  'zkpolygon-sepolia',\n  'fantom',\n  'fantom-testnet',\n  'glue', // Glue Mainnet - deprecated\n  'glue-testnet', // Glue Testnet - deprecated\n];\n\nexport const DEPRECATED_ENDPOINTS = [\n  40234, // venn-testnet\n  40158, // polygon zkevm\n  30218, // pgn network\n  10191, // aavegotchi testnet\n  166, // Moonriver\n  30215, // Horizen EON Mainnet V2 - deprecated\n  215, // Horizen EON Mainnet V1 - deprecated\n  10215, // Horizen EON Testnet V1 - deprecated\n  1,\n  2,\n  10,\n  11,\n  12,\n  14,\n  15,\n  16,\n  26,\n  210, // astar\n  10210, // astar-testnet\n  10220, // zKatana Astar zkEVM Testnet\n  10224, // Polygon CDK Testnet\n  218, // PGN network\n  10223, // Public Goods Network Testnet\n  10151, // metis testnet\n  10181, // mantle goerli testnet\n  10191, // Aavegotchi testnet\n  10109, // mumbai\n  10132, // optimism-goerli\n  10143, // arbitrum-goerli\n  10152, // intain\n  10234, // chainKey: venn-testnet\n  10237, // chainKey: xchain-testnet\n  10256, // old bera-testnet\n  40109, // polygon-mumbai\n  40143, // arbitrum goerli\n  40157, // linea goerli\n  40195, // wanchain-testnet,zora-testnet\n  40237, // xchain-testnet\n  40256, // old bera-testnet\n  50168, // solana-sandbox\n  50121, // ethereum-sandbox\n  50109, // polygon-sandbox\n  50102, // bsc-sandbox\n  20231,\n  20121,\n  20109,\n  20102,\n  30152, // intain\n  30114, // swimmer\n  40316, // treasure testnet old\n  40359, //